---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/blog-placeholder-about.jpg';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="Data scientist and AI engineer building toward agentic AI and insurtech, based in Accra, Ghana."
	pubDate={new Date('October 15 2026')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<p>
		I'm Akorfa — a data scientist and software engineer based in Accra, Ghana, working toward
		becoming an agentic AI engineer and, eventually, an AI solutions architect for insurtech.
	</p>

	<p>
		I hold a degree in Actuarial Science and have worked across data analysis, backend
		development, and machine learning — from A/B testing and data analysis at KudiPay Ghana to
		building a Django/PostgreSQL inventory backend at Eazzier Transpay. I'm currently pursuing a
		Software Development degree through BYU-Pathway and working through the AWS AI & ML Scholars
		Challenge on the Agentic Engineer track, building agents on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore.
	</p>

	<p>
		This blog is where I write about what I'm actually building: agentic AI systems, machine
		learning pipelines, and the engineering decisions behind them. I write about the bugs I hit,
		the trade-offs I made, and what I'd do differently — not polished tutorials, but honest
		build logs.
	</p>

	<p>
		My longer-term goal is to build AI-powered tools for African insurance and fintech markets.
		This blog is part of that path: a place to think in public, share what I'm learning, and
		build a record of the work before the company exists.
	</p>

	<p>
		You can find my code on <a href="https://github.com/akorfaa" target="_blank">GitHub</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>